From: EglantinePS5
Subject: [PATCH] up: EDEN_UP_SHADER_SET_WHY counts compute and task/mesh asks too (asked, served from the set, in the set but not prepared, refused, no record), on the timer

Switch: none new. Acts with EDEN_UP_SHADER_SET_WHY=1; compute asks only with
EDEN_UP_SHADER_SET_COMPUTE=1 (without it the set has no compute records). Off: nothing changes
(the totals line is the same; the new line prints only when a mesh or compute ask was seen).

Why: the WHY totals counted task/mesh asks only as "mesh=N" and compute asks not at all, so a
start with 0780-0783 on could not tell how many of its 59 mesh and 94 compute pipelines (d4) the
set served.

What:
- Mesh asks (the existing samples) are sorted like graphics ones besides the old count: served
  from the set, made from an own kept record, in the set but not prepared, in the set but refused
  (or the store closed), no record in the set. The catalogue already holds the mesh records' keys
  when EDEN_UP_SHADER_SET_MESH=1.
- Compute: the catalogue also reads the compute records' keys (keys only, as the store's
  KeptComputeHash), sorted. A dispatch that makes a new compute pipeline with the compute switch
  on notes one sample (key, what CreateKeptComputePipeline found in the store, made from it or
  not), at most 4,096 waiting; they are sorted with the graphics samples when the catalogue is
  ready.
- One more line beside the totals, from the same timer (EDEN_UP_SHADER_SET_WHY_EVERY_S, 0771),
  the minute line and the shutdown line: "EDEN_UP_SHADER_SET_WHY mesh and compute: mesh asked=
  served_from_set= own= in_set_not_prepared= in_set_refused= no_record=; compute asked= ... waiting=
  dropped=". Compute asks also move the "a count changed" test of the timer.
- The catalogue line names the compute records.

Needs 0771 and 0781. Checked: apply in name order, PS5-target syntax check. Not checked on the
console.
---
